  "body": [
    "Product Product Playbook 101 The next era of media storage Visual storage Dynamic space for all type of media. Smart search GPT-powered for results you can trust. Review & approval Comment & react in real-time Publish sites Create sites from stored files Mini-apps Supercharge your creative workflow Desktop sync Two-way file syncing Take a quick tour! See Playbook in action with our interactive product tour.",
    "API/SDK",
    "Solutions Use cases Enterprise Marketing Manage creative ops at scale with smart workflows. Media & Entertainment Manage production assets at scale with smart workflows. Creative Agency Collaborate with clients and streamline creative reviews. Consumer Brands Centralize brand assets and keep every team on brand. Game Studios Organize large game assets without paying twice for storage.",
    "Manage creative ops at scale with smart workflows.",
    "Manage production assets at scale with smart workflows.",
    "Collaborate with clients and streamline creative reviews.",
    "Centralize brand assets and keep every team on brand.",
    "Organize large game assets without paying twice for storage.",
    "Resources Resources Help center & tutorials Quick start guides and tutorials Customer stories Real examples. Real results. Portfolio showcase Featured creatives and projects Free giveaway 500+ illustrations from our community More to explore About us Story of Playbook Blog Privacy & ownership Browse template gallery 100+ stunning templates and featured examples from our community.",
    "Pricing",
    "Learn how to use the Playbook plugin for Figma to pull approved assets into a design",
    "The Playbook plugin for Figma puts your workspace inside the design file. Pull approved photography, logos and product shots straight onto the canvas, and send final exports back to a board when the work is done, without downloading and re-uploading anything.",
    "Install the Playbook plugin from the Figma community, then sign in to your Playbook workspace the first time you open it.",
    "Where it lives: open it from any Figma file through the plugin menu.",
    "One sign-in: the plugin remembers your workspace, so later files open straight into your boards.",
    "With a Figma file open, open the plugin and browse the boards you already have.",
    "Drag and drop: drag an asset from the plugin panel onto the canvas and it lands as a layer.",
    "Work from the real source: because you are pulling from the workspace rather than a local copy, the file on the canvas is the one the team approved.",
    "Other ways to move work in and out: Import syncs for cloud storage, and Canva for the same round trip in the Canva editor.",
